      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It is generally not recommended to mix Sertraline with daytime NyQuil because most NyQuil products contain codeine, which can interact with SSRIs and increase the risk of confusion, sleepiness, and low mood. Additionally, \"daytime\" formulations of cough medicines should avoid ingredients like dextromethorphan in combination with antidepressants, as this can cause serotonin syndrome or other dangerous side effects. Please consult your doctor or pharmacist immediately before taking any new medication to ensure there are no harmful interactions between your current dose of Sertraline and the other drugs.",
